  "observations": {
    "03-v4": [
      "Head, face, gourd and upper-body scale visually match 09-v4 and adjacent 04-v3. Hair top is y216 vs master y215; the enlarged 03-v2/v3 scale is no longer visible. Upper body was regenerated by the model, not promised pixel-identical.",
      "Anatomical right foot is below the pelvis with a visibly flat sole; left leg bends with its foot clear of the ground. Right empty fist swings forward, left hand retains the one gourd, headband knot stays anatomical left/viewer right.",
      "Alpha>=128 bottom-exclusive y1102 vs master y1098: the visible lower edge is 4 native pixels lower. This remains outside the strict requested ground-height limit.",
      "Best of this round because its flat support and near-master ground height are more useful than v5. Candidate for review only; do not silently mark the ground constraint passed."
    ],
    "03-v5": [
      "Head/body scale remains visually stable; hair top y217.",
      "Requested right boot move was 8 pixels upward, but output bottom is y1067: 35 pixels above v4 and 31 pixels above master. The shortened support leg creates a new fixed-ground continuity concern, so this version is not recommended."
    ],
    "02_to_03_to_04": [
      "02-v1 still appears to have a larger head/upper body than the fixed-scale 09-v4/03-v4/04-v3 group. Its alpha top is y131; 03-v4 y216; 04-v3 y215. These values alone do not measure head size or prove a motion defect, but the whole adjacent transition must be reviewed.",
      "Left knee passing and right-arm counter-swing are static candidate observations; their timing and 02-to-04 progression have not been dynamically verified."
    ]
